y and unaffected behaviour. Recheck after material deletion or simplification.\n    18\t\n    19\t**R6. Preserve trustworthy context.** Keep a canonical source where practical. Label drafts and assumptions; record decisions as decisions. Retain source and status when reusing information. Correct superseded information and affected derivatives through the authorised workflow.\n    20\t\n    21\t**R7. Learn from defects.** Fix the current result. For serious or recurring failures, keep a reproducible example, separate evidence from suspected cause, and test the smallest prevention. Prefer source, tool or check improvements over prompt prose. Retire obsolete rules, leaving their ID unused.\n    22\t\n    23\t## Model-Specific Delta Controls (gpt-6.2-sol)\n    24\t- D-SOL-1: End every non-capped engineering response with a `Blockers & Flaws` section listing every unresolved failed tool, missing input, unrun check, or unmet requirement (omit already-resolved retries; write `None` only when all checks passed). On direct length-bounded deliverables (briefs, memos, Slack handoffs, sign-offs), omit empty `Blockers & Flaws` footers and fold any real unresolved blocker inline within the requested word cap.\n    25\t- D-SOL-2: Verify against explicit `Invariants`, `Out-of-Scope`, and `Verify Command` blocks, emit `BLOCKED_SAFETY` verbatim rather than stubbing code on guardrail triggers, and limit PR review output to high-severity defects (<= 10 comments [Heuristic]).\nbenchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/tests/test_worker.py\nbenchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_description.md\nbenchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch\nbenchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts\nbenchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
